    At the risk of seeming trivial, poking my proposal in amongst the heated
discussions regarding sci.mil, rec.arts.cartoons, comp.sys.next, comp.os.mach,
comp.lang.sigplan, and comp.unix.microport and company, I hereby propose the
beginnings of discussion for the creation of the group rec.games.omega.
    I believe this was proposed once before, last year some time. The sugges-
tion was made to wait until the game was available to every site, by ftp from
the archives or some other method, for those who could not reach the author
or get comp.sources.games at their site. This is now the case. The traffic
volume in both rec.games.misc and comp.sources.games.bugs seems to me to be
high enough to justify this group's creation.
    Note that this is a call for discussion, not a call for votes. Followups
are directed to news.misc only. Please mail or post your thoughts on the sub-
ject.
